cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  isitfair: subgroup deployment-readiness auditing for clinical prediction
  models
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the companion
  paper below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guillen-Ramirez
    given-names: Hugo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0705-7432"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/HugoGuillen/isitfair
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-02
keywords:
  - fairness
  - clinical prediction models
  - calibration
  - decision curve analysis
  - TRIPOD+AI
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for fairness evaluation of clinical prediction models,
  built around the joint discrimination-calibration-clinical-utility
  framework. It produces TRIPOD+AI-aligned subgroup reports for trained
  binary-classification models, always reporting within-group performance
  alongside gap statistics, and enforces a single explicit rule for when a
  subgroup estimate is too sparse to carry an interval.
